; Brønsted-Lowry definition: acid donates H⁺, base accepts H⁺.
; Lewis definition (broader): acid accepts electron pair, base donates.
; 
; pH = -log[H⁺]. pH 7 = neutral. pH < 7 = acidic. pH > 7 = basic.
; water self-ionises: H2O ⇌ H⁺ + OH⁻  Kw = 10⁻¹⁴ at 25°C.
; strong acid: fully dissociates. HCl, H2SO4, HNO3.
; weak acid: partially dissociates. pKa measures strength.
; strong base: NaOH, KOH.
; weak base: NH3, amines.
; 
; neutralisation: acid + base → salt + water.
; HCl + NaOH → NaCl + H2O   ΔH = -57 kJ/mol (exothermic)
; CH3COOH + NaOH → CH3COONa + H2O
; 
; buffer: weak acid + conjugate base. resists pH change.
; Henderson-Hasselbalch: pH = pKa + log([A⁻]/[HA]).
; blood pH 7.4 maintained by carbonate buffer (H2CO3/HCO3⁻).
; 
; amino acids are amphoteric — can act as acid or base.
; at physiological pH they exist as zwitterions (+NH3 and COO⁻).
; proteins fold based partly on electrostatic interactions at physiological pH.

